> Check the three transforms on supplied pixels

Domain0 keeps the image,1 computes1-image, and2 rotates by90 degrees with
out(y,x)=original(H-1-x,y), without inversion. The reusable native transform
accepts signed square grayscale NHWC inputs and per-row integer0..2 codes;
it does not clip or fit anything. The following2x2 pixels are supplied binary
fractions. They make the orientation visible before any dataset is loaded.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_domain_toy.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto x      = n::tensor({0., .25, .5, .75}, {1, 2, 2, 1}, n::DType::Float64);
  auto all    = n::models::StarDomainImages(
      n::tile(x, {3, 1, 1, 1}), n::tensor({0, 1, 2}, {3}, n::DType::Int64));
  if (!n::equal_bits(
          n::take_rows(all, {2}), n::tensor({.5, 0., .75, .25}, {1, 2, 2, 1}, x.dtype())))
    throw std::runtime_error("rotation orientation");
  n::save_image_grid(all, "build/star_domain_toy.png", 3, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 60);
}
```
