> Select disjoint identities by occurrence order and keep unused IDs

For each digit, the first30 fitting observations enter domain0, next30 domain1,
next30 domain2, leaving10 unused. With100 observations per digit this selects
900/1000 fitting rows. Held-out pools use6 per class/domain, selecting180/200.
All selected and unused IDs preserve the original global row order. Original
pixels remain available exactly for diagnostics; images are transformed only
after selection. The checked native loader supplies cross-pool provenance and
pixel-uniqueness checks; the split helper itself validates balanced metadata,
unit pixels and unique nonnegative IDs within its supplied pool.

The toy below uses40 supplied IDs, four occurrences per digit, and per_class1.
The fourth occurrence remains explicitly unused. Placeholder images are zeros;
this toy explains identity selection and makes no pixel-uniqueness claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_partition_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n             = dm::nn;
  auto labels             = n::cast(n::arange(0, 40, 1, n::DType::Float64) / 4., n::DType::Int64),
       ids                = n::arange(100, 140, 1, n::DType::Int64);
  auto                out = n::models::SplitStarDomains(n::zeros({40, 28, 28, 1}), labels, ids, 1);
  std::vector<double> selected = out.source.to_vector<double>(),
                      domain   = out.domain.to_vector<double>(),
                      unused   = out.unused.to_vector<double>(), height(unused.size(), 3);
  auto p                       = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-.5, 5.5)
      .points(selected, domain, "Selected domain0/1/2", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .points(unused, height, "Unused original IDs", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .x_label("Supplied original source identity, preserved in global order")
      .y_label("Assigned domain; unused shown separately at3")
      .title("Three disjoint occurrences per digit, plus explicit unused IDs")
      .save_svg("build/star_partition_toy.svg");
}
```
