> Separate stable three-domain cross entropy from source patch scores

StarDomainLoss uses mean(-sum(one_hot(target,3)*log_softmax(logits),classes)).
Zero logits give log(3). For supplied logits(1000,-1000,0) and target1 it gives
2000 with partials(1,-1,0), without probability clipping or overflow. Domain
IDs are checked before one-hot construction. The plot varies logit0 while the
other two logits stay zero, showing CE for requested domains0 and1. It uses no
fitted data. The raw source head is a separate least-squares map, not this CE.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_ce_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n  = dm::nn;
  auto t       = n::DType::Float64;
  auto extreme = n::tensor({1000., -1000., 0.}, {1, 3}, t).requires_grad_();
  auto loss    = n::models::StarDomainLoss(extreme, n::ones({1}, n::DType::Int64));
  auto partial = n::grad(loss, {extreme})[0];
  if (loss.item() != 2000 || partial.at({0, 0}) != 1 || partial.at({0, 1}) != -1)
    throw std::runtime_error("stable extreme CE");
  std::vector<double> x, a, b;
  for (int i = 0; i <= 40; ++i) {
    double value  = -4. + i * .2;
    auto   logits = n::tensor({value, 0., 0.}, {1, 3}, t);
    x.push_back(value);
    a.push_back(n::models::StarDomainLoss(logits, n::zeros({1}, n::DType::Int64)).item());
    b.push_back(n::models::StarDomainLoss(logits, n::ones({1}, n::DType::Int64)).item());
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(0, 8)
      .lines(x, a, "Requested domain0", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(x, b, "Requested domain1", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .x_label("Supplied domain logit0; logits1/2 fixed at0")
      .y_label("Native stable cross entropy")
      .title("A domain head is trained against its explicit integer target")
      .save_svg("build/star_ce_toy.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/star_ce_toy.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Both41-point curves retain the entire supplied logit sweep. Domain0 becomes cheaper as its own logit rises; domain1 becomes more expensive.)
\alttext(Two41-sample cross-entropy curves compare requested classes0 and1 as only logit0 varies.)

> Keep both uses of the shared generator in the reconstruction derivative

A small supplied model makes the shared path checkable: g(x,t)=a*x+b*t,
x=.25,b=.2,t=1,original=0, loss=(g(g(x,t),0)-x)^2. At a=.5, fake=.325,
reconstruction=.1625 and dloss/da=-.07875. Treating fake as detached gives
-.056875, even though reconstruction pixels are identical. The actual native
StarGAN tests check the same distinction through the full U-Net.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_shared_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n           = dm::nn;
  auto                t = n::DType::Float64;
  std::vector<double> x, full, stopped;
  for (int i = 0; i <= 40; ++i) {
    double value          = i / 40.;
    auto   a              = n::full({}, value, t).requires_grad_();
    auto   fake           = a * .25 + .2;
    auto   reconstruction = a * fake;
    auto   loss           = n::square(reconstruction - .25);
    auto   correct        = n::grad(loss, {a})[0];
    auto   wrong          = n::grad(n::square(a * fake.detach() - .25), {a})[0];
    x.push_back(value);
    full.push_back(correct.item());
    stopped.push_back(wrong.item());
    if (i == 20 &&
        (std::abs(correct.item() + .07875) > 1e-14 || std::abs(wrong.item() + .056875) > 1e-14))
      throw std::runtime_error("both G paths");
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-.15, .55)
      .lines(x, full, "Both shared uses", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(x, stopped, "Detached fake control", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .x_label("Supplied shared generator coefficient a")
      .y_label("Reconstruction loss partial with respect to a")
      .title("Identical forward pixels can have different shared-G partials")
      .save_svg("build/star_shared_toy.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/star_shared_toy.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All41 coefficient values are retained. The detached control is explanatory only; the actual experiment keeps both generator paths live.)
\alttext(Two41-point derivative curves compare both shared uses of one scalar generator with an incorrectly detached intermediate.)

> Preserve each objective scale and the critic-then-fresh-generator schedule

G=(full fake-to1 patch mean+fake-domain CE)+10*roundtrip meanL1.
D=.5*(real-to1 patch mean+fake-to0 patch mean)+real-domain CE. There is no
fake-domain CE in D loss, and no half on G's source term. At all-zero source
and domain logits, source losses are G1/D.5 and CE is log(3). The toy below
sets a supplied reconstruction error to.25, so complete G=1+log(3)+2.5 and
D=.5+log(3). Known transformed targets are diagnostics only.

Each fitting batch captures and applies D first, then makes a fresh G forward
through updated D using the same source/original/target batch. Separate Adam
states own the two stores. A stale pre-D G capture changes the method; the saved
first-batch control quantifies it later. No API hides captures or optimizer writes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto zero   = n::zeros({2, 7, 7, 1}),
       ce     = n::models::StarDomainLoss(n::zeros({2, 3}), n::zeros({2}, n::DType::Int64));
  auto g      = (n::mean(n::square(zero - 1.)) + ce) + 10. * n::mean(n::full({2, 28, 28, 1}, .25));
  auto d      = .5 * (n::mean(n::square(zero - 1.)) + n::mean(n::square(zero))) + ce;
  std::print(
      "| Supplied zero-head control | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Three-domain CE | {} |\n| G with "
      "reconstruction L1.25 | {} |\n| D | {} |\n",
      ce.item(),
      g.item(),
      d.item());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Supplied zero-head control | Value |
|---|---:|
| Three-domain CE | 1.0986123085021973 |
| G with reconstruction L1.25 | 4.598612308502197 |
| D | 1.5986123085021973 |
// result_end
> Trace the actual conditioned U-Net and shared critic trunk

The generator tiles a three-way one-hot target over28x28 and concatenates it
after the source channel. Two biased normal(.02)4x4/stride2 ReLU maps4→4→8
encode14x14 then7x7. Learned transposes decode8→4, concatenate(up14,down14),
then8→2. The final skip concatenates(up28,full conditioned input), six channels,
before the3x3 sigmoid output. There is no normalization, dropout or noise.
For the single-input plotting interface only, the trace packs source pixels
and the supplied integer domain into785 values; it slices/casts that code
before the native call. The production API keeps source and target separate.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_generator_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore g(6301);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& packed) {
        auto source = n::reshape(n::slice(packed, {0, 0}, {1, 784}), {1, 28, 28, 1});
        auto target = n::cast(n::reshape(n::slice(packed, {0, 784}, {1, 1}), {1}), n::DType::Int64);
        n::model_stage("Supplied source", packed, source);
        auto o = n::models::StarGanGenerate(g, source, target);
        n::model_stage("Supplied target: tile one-hot3", packed, o.code);
        n::model_stage(
            "Concat source,target code", std::vector<n::Tensor>{source, o.code}, o.input);
        n::model_stage("Down4x4/2 ReLU4 to4", o.input, o.down14);
        n::model_stage("Down4x4/2 ReLU4 to8", o.down14, o.down7);
        n::model_stage("Transpose8 to4 ReLU", o.down7, o.up14);
        n::model_stage("Concat up14,down14", std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.up14, o.down14}, o.joined14);
        n::model_stage("Transpose8 to2 ReLU", o.joined14, o.up28);
        n::model_stage(
            "Concat up28,full condition", std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.up28, o.input}, o.joined28);
        return n::model_stage("Conv3x3 sigmoid6 to1", o.joined28, o.image);
      },
      "StarGAN G: requested-domain code in both real skips");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 4;
  auto fig                      = model.plot(n::ones({1, 785}), options);
  if (fig.parameter_count() != 1609 || g.size() != 10)
    throw std::runtime_error("G source census");
  fig.save_svg("build/star_generator_architecture.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/star_generator_architecture.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The executed trace uses1609 values in10 leaves and both actual skip joins. Target codes are discrete data, not learned parameters or paired target images.)
\alttext(An executed28→14→7→14→28 generator diagram keeps the one-hot target producer and both conditioned skip concatenations.)

The image-only critic uses normal(.02)4x4/stride2 maps1→4→8, each followed
by LeakyReLU(.2). Spatial mean of the7x7 trunk feeds a Glorot8→3 domain head;
a separate normal3x3 head yields49 raw source scores. The domain head initializes
before the source head to preserve seed6311's stream and names:688 values in8
leaves. Its raw source patches have nominal18x18 receptive fields, including
zero padding near borders. The next trace retains both heads, returning their
concatenation solely to make both visible in a single-output diagram.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_critic_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore d(6311);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& image) {
        auto o = n::models::StarGanDiscriminate(d, image);
        n::model_stage("Down4x4/2 leaky1 to4", image, o.down14);
        n::model_stage("Down4x4/2 leaky4 to8", o.down14, o.down7);
        n::model_stage("Spatial mean + domain dense3", o.down7, o.domain_logits);
        n::model_stage("Raw source3x3 8 to1", o.down7, o.source);
        auto flattened = n::reshape(o.source, {1, 49});
        return n::model_stage(
            "Both raw heads, diagnostic trace",
            std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.source, o.domain_logits},
            n::concat({flattened, o.domain_logits}, 1));
      },
      "StarGAN D: image-only shared trunk and two heads");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 4;
  auto fig                      = model.plot(n::ones({1, 28, 28, 1}), options);
  if (fig.parameter_count() != 688 || d.size() != 8)
    throw std::runtime_error("D source census");
  fig.save_svg("build/star_critic_architecture.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/star_critic_architecture.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The executed critic trace has688 unique learned values. The production function exposes raw source/domain fields and domain softmax separately; no domain code enters D.)
\alttext(A shared image-only convolution trunk branches into spatially pooled three-domain logits and a7x7 raw source head.)

> Run the complete native experiment with every fitting action visible

The native loader prepares/checks MNIST saliency pools, then SplitStarDomains
selects the three disjoint domains. Gseed6301/Dseed6311 initialize once. Batch
order6323 visits all900 fitting rows per epoch;29 batches include the last4
rows. Each epoch draws uniform target IDs from raw MTseed6337+epoch, rejecting
4294967295 before modulo3; accepted raw words are saved. These targets need
not differ from the original domain. Fixed validation/test targets are
(original+1)%3. Three epochs give87 writes per owner,174 total. Adam is
(.0002,beta1.5,beta2.999,epsilon1e-8), with no hidden extra update.

Every epoch records validation, but selection stays at the fixed final epoch.
The program saves every phase partial and after-state, all source outputs,
accepted target words, stale-G control and restored inference checks. The
additional domain means use fitting rows only; known target mappings stay
outside the game and serve only MSE diagnostics. The balanced gallery includes
all ten digits in every source domain without filtering generated results.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <chrono>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
namespace nn = dm::nn;
namespace m  = nn::models;
using nn::Tensor;
using Arrays = std::map<std::string, Tensor>;
void Require(bool ok, const std::string& why) {
  if (!ok)
    throw std::runtime_error(why);
}
void SaveArrays(const std::string& path, const Arrays& a) {
  nn::save_npz(path, nn::NamedTensors(a.begin(), a.end()));
}
Tensor Rows(const Tensor& x, const std::vector<std::int64_t>& rows) {
  return nn::take_rows(x, rows);
}
Tensor Flat784(const Tensor& x) {
  return nn::reshape(x, {-1, 784});
}
void Mosaic(const std::filesystem::path& path, const Tensor& image, std::int64_t columns) {
  nn::save_image_grid(
      nn::reshape(image, {-1, 28, 28, 1}), path.string(), columns, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
}
bool BitEqual(const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
  return nn::equal_bits(a, b);
}
bool BitEqual(const Arrays& a, const Arrays& b) {
  if (a.size() != b.size())
    return false;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
    if (!b.count(k) || !BitEqual(v, b.at(k)))
      return false;
  return true;
}
double MaxAbsDiff(const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
  return nn::max(nn::abs(nn::cast(a, nn::DType::Float64) - nn::cast(b, nn::DType::Float64))).item();
}
Arrays Fields(const m::StarGanOutput& o) {
  return {
      {"fake", o.fake},
      {"reconstruction", o.reconstruction},
      {"real_source", o.real_source},
      {"fake_source", o.fake_source},
      {"real_domain_logits", o.real_domain_logits},
      {"fake_domain_logits", o.fake_domain_logits},
      {"real_domain_probability", o.real_domain_probability},
      {"fake_domain_probability", o.fake_domain_probability},
      {"source_loss_g", o.source_loss_g},
      {"source_loss_d", o.source_loss_d},
      {"real_domain_loss", o.real_domain_loss},
      {"fake_domain_loss", o.fake_domain_loss},
      {"reconstruction_loss", o.reconstruction_loss},
      {"generator_loss", o.generator_loss},
      {"discriminator_loss", o.discriminator_loss}};
}
void Initialize(nn::ParameterStore& g, nn::ParameterStore& d) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto fake = m::StarGanGenerate(g, nn::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1}), nn::zeros({1}, nn::DType::Int32));
  m::StarGanDiscriminate(d, fake.image);
}
Arrays Snapshot(const std::vector<nn::ParameterStore*>& p) {
  Arrays a;
  for (int k = 0; k < 2; ++k)
    for (const auto& name : p[k]->names())
      a.emplace(std::to_string(k) + "/" + name, p[k]->at(name).detach().clone());
  return a;
}
void Restore(const std::vector<nn::ParameterStore*>& p, const std::string& path) {
  auto a = nn::load_npz(path);
  Require(a.size() == 18, "complete18-leaf checkpoint");
  for (const auto& [key, value] : a) {
    Require(
        key.size() > 2 && (key[0] == '0' || key[0] == '1') && key[1] == '/',
        "known checkpoint prefix");
    auto& owner = *p[key[0] - '0'];
    Require(
        owner.contains(key.substr(2)) && owner.at(key.substr(2)).shape() == value.shape(),
        "known matching checkpoint leaf");
    owner.set(key.substr(2), value);
  }
}
std::vector<Tensor> Ordered(nn::ParameterStore& p, int group, const Arrays& a) {
  std::vector<Tensor> out;
  for (const auto& name : p.names())
    out.push_back(a.at(std::to_string(group) + "/" + name));
  return out;
}
void RequireOnlyOwnersChanged(
    const Arrays&                   a,
    const Arrays&                   b,
    const std::vector<std::string>& prefixes,
    const std::string&              why,
    bool                            require_change) {
  bool changed = false;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : a) {
    bool selected = false;
    for (const auto& prefix : prefixes)
      selected |= key.starts_with(prefix);
    if (!BitEqual(value, b.at(key))) {
      Require(selected, why);
      changed = true;
    }
  }
  if (require_change)
    Require(changed, why + " changes selected store");
}
Tensor Generate(nn::ParameterStore& g, const Tensor& x, const Tensor& t) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  return m::StarGanGenerate(g, x, t).image;
}
Arrays Classify(nn::ParameterStore& d, const Tensor& x) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto            out = m::StarGanDiscriminate(d, x);
  return {{"source", out.source}, {"domain_probability", out.domain_probability}};
}
namespace {

double Value(const Arrays& a, const std::string& key) {
  return a.at(key).item();
}
std::vector<std::int32_t> Ints(const Tensor& t) {
  return nn::cast(t, nn::DType::Int32).contiguous().to_vector<std::int32_t>();
}
Tensor IntTensor(const std::vector<std::int32_t>& v) {
  return nn::from_vector(v, {std::int64_t(v.size())});
}

/// Domain 0 = original, 1 = 1 - x, 2 = rotated (out(y, x) = in(27 - x, y)).
Tensor DomainImages(const Tensor& original, const Tensor& domain) {
  return m::StarDomainImages(original, domain);
}

/// Uniform domains v % 3 from std::mt19937(seed), rejecting 2^32 - 1; also the raw draws.
std::pair<Tensor, Tensor> Targets(int n, std::uint32_t seed) {
  auto out = m::UniformCategorical(n, seed);
  return {out.labels, out.raw};
}
Tensor NextDomain(const Tensor& original) {
  auto d = Ints(original);
  for (auto& v : d)
    v = (v + 1) % 3;
  return IntTensor(d);
}
std::int64_t Argmax(const std::vector<float>& p, std::int64_t row) {
  std::int64_t best = 0;
  for (int c = 1; c < 3; ++c)
    if (p[row * 3 + c] > p[row * 3 + best])
      best = c;
  return best;
}

void Run(
    const std::filesystem::path& data,
    const std::filesystem::path& root,
    int                          epochs,
    const std::string&           init) {
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  const auto probe_root = root;
  std::filesystem::create_directories(probe_root / "phases");
  const auto                  originals = m::LoadSaliency(data);
  std::vector<m::StarDomains> pools;
  Arrays                      records;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    pools.push_back(
        m::SplitStarDomains(
            originals[k].images, originals[k].labels, originals[k].source, k == 0 ? 30 : 6));
    const std::string name = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    records.emplace(name + "_all_original", originals[k].images);
    records.emplace(name + "_all_digit", originals[k].labels);
    records.emplace(name + "_all_source_ids", originals[k].source);
    records.emplace(name + "_images", pools[k].image);
    records.emplace(name + "_original", pools[k].original);
    records.emplace(name + "_domains", pools[k].domain);
    records.emplace(name + "_digits", pools[k].digit);
    records.emplace(name + "_source_ids", pools[k].source);
    records.emplace(name + "_unused_source_ids", pools[k].unused);
  }
  SaveArrays((root / "data.npz").string(), records);
  const Tensor vt = NextDomain(pools[1].domain), tt = NextDomain(pools[2].domain);
  SaveArrays((root / "fixed_targets.npz").string(), {{"validation", vt}, {"test", tt}});
  nn::ParameterStore               g(6301), d(6311);
  std::vector<nn::ParameterStore*> stores{&g, &d};
  Initialize(g, d);
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind    = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  config.beta1   = .5;
  config.beta2   = .999;
  config.epsilon = 1e-8;
  nn::Optimizer               go(g, .0002, config), do_(d, .0002, config);
  std::vector<nn::Optimizer*> optimizers{&go, &do_};
  auto                        evaluate = [&](const Tensor& x, const Tensor& o, const Tensor& t) {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    return Fields(m::StarGan(g, d, x, o, t));
  };
  auto capture = [&](int group, const Tensor& x, const Tensor& o, const Tensor& t) {
    // Always fresh: the G capture below observes the D write from this batch.
    auto out     = m::StarGan(g, d, x, o, t);
    auto partial = nn::grad(
        group == 0 ? out.generator_loss : out.discriminator_loss, stores[group]->parameters());
    Arrays result;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < partial.size(); ++i)
      result.emplace(std::to_string(group) + "/" + stores[group]->names()[i], partial[i]);
    return result;
  };
  if (!init.empty())
    Restore(stores, init);
  Require(
      g.count() == 1609 && d.count() == 688 && g.size() + d.size() == 18, "2297 params 18 tensors");
  SaveArrays((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), Snapshot(stores));
  SaveArrays(
      (root / "initial_outputs.npz").string(), evaluate(pools[2].image, pools[2].domain, tt));
  nn::BatchOrder order(900, 32, 6323);
  int            steps = 0;
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history << "epoch\tdiscriminator_loss\tgenerator_loss\treal_domain_loss\tfake_domain_"
             "loss\treconstruction_loss\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto source = Ints(pools[0].source);
  Tensor     first_x, first_original, first_target;
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    const auto targets = Targets(900, 6337 + epoch);
    SaveArrays(
        (probe_root / ("probe-targets" + std::to_string(epoch) + ".npz")).string(),
        {{"target", targets.first}, {"raw", targets.second}});
    order.begin_epoch();
    for (;;) {
      const auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      const Tensor x = Rows(pools[0].image, rows), original = Rows(pools[0].domain, rows),
                   target = Rows(targets.first, rows);
      if (!steps) {
        first_x        = x;
        first_original = original;
        first_target   = target;
        SaveArrays(
            (probe_root / "probe-first-input.npz").string(),
            {{"x", x}, {"original", original}, {"target", target}});
        SaveArrays(
            (probe_root / "probe-first-forward.npz").string(), evaluate(x, original, target));
        SaveArrays(
            (probe_root / "probe-stale-g-gradient.npz").string(), capture(0, x, original, target));
      }
      for (int group : {1, 0}) {
        const auto before  = Snapshot(stores);
        const auto partial = capture(group, x, original, target);
        const auto name    = "batch" + std::to_string(steps) + (group == 1 ? "-d" : "-g");
        SaveArrays((probe_root / "phases" / (name + "-gradient.npz")).string(), partial);
        optimizers[group]->step(Ordered(*stores[group], group, partial));
        SaveArrays((probe_root / "phases" / (name + "-after.npz")).string(), Snapshot(stores));
        RequireOnlyOwnersChanged(
            before,
            Snapshot(stores),
            {std::to_string(group) + "/"},
            "each StarGAN step updates ONLY own group",
            !steps);
      }
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << steps << '\t' << row << '\t' << source[row] << '\n';
      ++steps;
    }
    SaveArrays(
        (probe_root / ("probe-epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + ".npz")).string(), Snapshot(stores));
    SaveArrays(
        (probe_root / ("probe-epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "-test.npz")).string(),
        evaluate(pools[2].image, pools[2].domain, tt));
    const auto v = evaluate(pools[1].image, pools[1].domain, vt);
    SaveArrays(
        (probe_root / ("probe-epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "-validation.npz")).string(), v);
    history << epoch;
    for (auto key :
         {"discriminator_loss",
          "generator_loss",
          "real_domain_loss",
          "fake_domain_loss",
          "reconstruction_loss"})
      history << '\t' << Value(v, key);
    history << '\n';
    std::cout << "epoch " << epoch << ": D=" << Value(v, "discriminator_loss")
              << ", G=" << Value(v, "generator_loss")
              << ", reconstruction L1=" << Value(v, "reconstruction_loss") << std::endl;
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();
  const auto checkpoint = (root / "final.npz").string();
  SaveArrays(checkpoint, Snapshot(stores));
  for (int group = 0; group < 2; ++group)
    SaveArrays(
        (root / ("final_gradients_group" + std::to_string(group) + ".npz")).string(),
        capture(group, first_x, first_original, first_target));
  nn::ParameterStore restored_g(1), restored_d(2);
  Initialize(restored_g, restored_d);
  std::vector<nn::ParameterStore*> restored{&restored_g, &restored_d};
  Restore(restored, checkpoint);
  nn::NoGradGuard inference_guard; // All following controls are read-only.
  auto            deployed_evaluate = [&](const Tensor& x, const Tensor& o, const Tensor& t) {
    return Fields(m::StarGan(restored_g, restored_d, x, o, t));
  };
  Require(
      BitEqual(Snapshot(stores), Snapshot(restored)), "all G/D source-domain heads restore exact");
  const auto   before     = Snapshot(restored);
  const auto   output     = deployed_evaluate(pools[2].image, pools[2].domain, tt);
  const Tensor prediction = Generate(restored_g, pools[2].image, tt);
  Require(BitEqual(prediction, output.at("fake")), "source + target domain ONLY generation exact");
  const auto classify = Classify(restored_d, pools[2].image);
  Require(
      BitEqual(classify.at("source"), output.at("real_source")) &&
          BitEqual(classify.at("domain_probability"), output.at("real_domain_probability")),
      "IMAGE ONLY D without domain/noise feed exact");
  const double parity = MaxAbsDiff(
      Generate(restored_g, Rows(pools[2].image, {0}), Rows(tt, {0})), Rows(prediction, {0}));
  Require(parity < 2e-6, "single batch parity");
  std::vector<std::int32_t> all(180, 0);
  const Tensor              p0 = Generate(restored_g, pools[2].image, IntTensor(all));
  std::fill(all.begin(), all.end(), 1);
  const Tensor p1 = Generate(restored_g, pools[2].image, IntTensor(all));
  std::fill(all.begin(), all.end(), 2);
  const Tensor p2            = Generate(restored_g, pools[2].image, IntTensor(all));
  const double domain_effect = std::max(MaxAbsDiff(p0, p1), MaxAbsDiff(p0, p2));
  Require(domain_effect > 1e-5, "target domain changes G pixels");
  int rejected = 0;
  for (int invalid : {-1, 3}) {
    std::fill(all.begin(), all.end(), 0);
    all[0] = invalid;
    try {
      Generate(restored_g, pools[2].image, IntTensor(all));
    } catch (const std::exception&) {
      ++rejected;
    }
  }
  try {
    Generate(restored_g, pools[2].image, Rows(tt, {0}));
  } catch (const std::exception&) {
    ++rejected;
  }
  Require(rejected == 3, "invalid domains rejected before one hot");
  Require(BitEqual(before, Snapshot(restored)), "all inference immutable");
  SaveArrays((root / "outputs.npz").string(), output);
  SaveArrays(
      (root / "domain_controls.npz").string(),
      {{"target0_prediction", p0},
       {"target1_prediction", p1},
       {"target2_prediction", p2},
       {"image_only_source", classify.at("source")},
       {"image_only_domain_probability", classify.at("domain_probability")}});
  const Tensor known = DomainImages(pools[2].original, tt);
  SaveArrays((root / "diagnostic_known_mapping.npz").string(), {{"target", known}});
  const double mse =
      nn::mean(
          nn::square(
              nn::cast(prediction, nn::DType::Float64) - nn::cast(known, nn::DType::Float64)))
          .item();
  double     real_accuracy = 0, fake_accuracy = 0;
  const auto rp     = output.at("real_domain_probability").contiguous().to_vector<float>(),
             fp     = output.at("fake_domain_probability").contiguous().to_vector<float>();
  const auto domain = Ints(pools[2].domain), targets = Ints(tt), digits = Ints(pools[2].digit);
  for (int b = 0; b < 180; ++b)
    real_accuracy += Argmax(rp, b) == domain[b], fake_accuracy += Argmax(fp, b) == targets[b];
  std::vector<std::int32_t> gallery_ids;
  std::vector<Tensor>       gallery_rows;
  for (int d = 0; d < 3; ++d)
    for (int digit = 0; digit < 3; ++digit) {
      int row = -1;
      for (int b = 0; b < 180 && row < 0; ++b)
        if (domain[b] == d && digits[b] == digit)
          row = b;
      Require(row >= 0, "first sample per 3x3 source-domain/digit grid");
      gallery_ids.push_back(row);
      for (const Tensor* t : std::vector<const Tensor*>{
               &pools[2].image, &p0, &p1, &p2, &output.at("reconstruction"), &known})
        gallery_rows.push_back(Flat784(Rows(*t, {row})));
    }
  const Tensor gallery = nn::concat(gallery_rows, 0);
  SaveArrays(
      (root / "gallery.npz").string(), {{"images", gallery}, {"rows", IntTensor(gallery_ids)}});
  Mosaic(root / "all_domains.png", gallery, 6);
  Require(go.iterations() == 87 && do_.iterations() == 87, "87 explicit Adam writes per owner");
  // A stronger diagnostic reference estimates each target-domain mean from fit rows only.
  std::vector<Tensor> means;
  for (int domain = 0; domain < 3; ++domain) {
    std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
    auto                      code = Ints(pools[0].domain);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < code.size(); ++i)
      if (code[i] == domain)
        rows.push_back(i);
    means.push_back(nn::mean(nn::cast(Rows(pools[0].image, rows), nn::DType::Float64), {0}));
  }
  const Tensor mean_bank       = nn::stack(means, 0),
               mean_prediction = nn::take_rows(
                   mean_bank, nn::cast(tt, nn::DType::Int64).to_vector<std::int64_t>());
  auto mse_ref = [&](const Tensor& image) {
    return nn::mean(
               nn::square(
                   nn::cast(image, nn::DType::Float64) - nn::cast(known, nn::DType::Float64)))
        .item();
  };
  SaveArrays(
      (root / "probe-fitting-mean-baseline.npz").string(),
      {{"means", mean_bank},
       {"prediction", mean_prediction},
       {"mse",
        nn::tensor(
            {mse_ref(prediction), mse_ref(mean_prediction), mse_ref(pools[2].image)},
            {3},
            nn::DType::Float64)}});
  std::vector<Tensor>       balanced;
  std::vector<std::int32_t> selected;
  for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; ++digit)
    for (int domain = 0; domain < 3; ++domain) {
      int  row   = -1;
      auto label = Ints(pools[2].digit), codes = Ints(pools[2].domain);
      for (int i = 0; i < 180 && row < 0; ++i)
        if (label[i] == digit && codes[i] == domain)
          row = i;
      Require(row >= 0, "ten-class three-domain gallery");
      selected.push_back(row);
      for (const Tensor* image : std::vector<const Tensor*>{&pools[2].image, &prediction, &known})
        balanced.push_back(Rows(*image, {row}));
    }
  const auto balanced_image = nn::concat(balanced, 0);
  SaveArrays(
      (root / "probe-balanced-gallery.npz").string(),
      {{"images", balanced_image}, {"rows", IntTensor(selected)}});
  Mosaic(root / "balanced.png", balanced_image, 9);
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":2297,\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"steps_per_group\":" << steps
       << ",\"optimizer_updates\":" << 2 * steps << ",\"selected_epoch_fixed_final\":" << epochs
       << ",\"diagnostic_known_mapping_mse\":" << mse
       << ",\"test_real_domain_accuracy\":" << real_accuracy / 180
       << ",\"test_generated_requested_domain_accuracy\":" << fake_accuracy / 180
       << ",\"target_domain_pixel_max_effect\":" << domain_effect
       << ",\"single_batch_max_error\":" << parity
       << ",\"invalid_domain_controls_rejected\":" << rejected;
  for (auto key :
       {"discriminator_loss",
        "generator_loss",
        "source_loss_g",
        "source_loss_d",
        "real_domain_loss",
        "fake_domain_loss",
        "reconstruction_loss"})
    meta << ",\"test_" << key << "\":" << Value(output, key);
  meta << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";
  Require(bool(meta) && bool(history) && bool(batches), "complete StarGAN records");
  std::cout << "fixed final=" << epochs
            << ", real/generated domain accuracy=" << real_accuracy / 180 << "/"
            << fake_accuracy / 180 << ", mapping MSE=" << mse
            << ", test D/G=" << Value(output, "discriminator_loss") << "/"
            << Value(output, "generator_loss")
            << "; single G/3 domains/classifier/roundtrip/restore/immutable PASS (training "
            << seconds << " s)\nArtifacts: " << root.string() << "\nAll star_gan checks passed.\n";
}

} // namespace

int main() {
  auto data = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency";
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", data.parent_path());
  Run(data, "build/star_gan", 3, "");
}
```
