> Preserve the original gallery and extend coverage to all ten digits

The original gallery selects the first digit0,1,2 observation in each source
domain. Its six columns are source, requested domain0, requested1, requested2,
reconstruction through original code, and known target for the fixed next-domain
request. The three generated-domain columns are counterfactual requests from
the same source row; the known mapping is supplied only for diagnosis.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_original_gallery.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
