> Retain every target-conditioning effect and the stale-gradient control

The original all-domain control evaluates each test source with target0,1,2.
Its maximum pixel effect is.1486200988. The next curve keeps every test row's
maximum absolute change between target0 and either alternative target, sorted
for display. This measures sensitivity to the requested code, not correct
translation or digit fidelity. No row is removed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_domain_effects.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace m = n::models;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& path) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz(path))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  return a;
}
int main() {
  auto a      = Read("build/star_gan/domain_controls.npz");
  auto effect = n::maximum(
      n::abs(a.at("target0_prediction") - a.at("target1_prediction")),
      n::abs(a.at("target0_prediction") - a.at("target2_prediction")));
  auto y = n::max(n::reshape(effect, {180, 784}), {1}).to_vector<double>();
  std::sort(y.begin(), y.end());
  std::vector<double> x(180);
  std::iota(x.begin(), x.end(), 1.);
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(0, .24)
      .lines(x, y, "Domain effect", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .x_label("Sorted test row index, all180 source rows")
      .y_label("Maximum absolute pixel change among target-code controls")
      .title("Every source retains its requested-domain sensitivity")
      .save_svg("build/star_domain_effects.svg");
}
