On the first real training batch, capturing G before D's update changes the
G partial vector by at most.00003471970558 compared with the required fresh
capture after D's write. Every one of the1609 G coordinates is plotted below,
ordered by sorted tensor key then row-major coordinate. This is a partial-vector
difference, not an extra parameter update. The actual run applies the fresh
vector only.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/star_stale_gradient.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace m = n::models;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& path) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz(path))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  return a;
}
int main() {
  auto stale = Read("build/star_gan/probe-stale-g-gradient.npz"),
       fresh = Read("build/star_gan/phases/batch0-g-gradient.npz");
  std::vector<n::Tensor> values;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : stale)
    values.push_back(
        n::reshape(
            n::abs(n::cast(value, n::DType::Float64) - n::cast(fresh.at(key), n::DType::Float64)),
            {-1}));
  auto delta = n::concat(values, 0);
  if (delta.numel() != 1609 || std::abs(n::max(delta).item() - 3.471970558166504e-5) > 1e-15)
    throw std::runtime_error("stale source G control");
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-2, 70)
      .lines(
          n::arange(0, 1609, 1, n::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>(),
          (delta * 1e6).to_vector<double>(),
          "Stale vs fresh G",
          {37, 99, 235},
          1.3)
      .x_label("G partial coordinate; sorted source keys then row-major values")
      .y_label("Absolute first-batch G partial change, multiplied by1e6")
      .title("Fresh G through updated D is part of the method")
      .save_svg("build/star_stale_gradient.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/star_stale_gradient.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All1609 coordinates remain, including zeros. Vertical units multiply the raw partial difference by1e6 for readable ticks. D and G retain independent Adam states and87 writes each.)
\alttext(A1609-coordinate absolute-difference curve shows the saved stale generator vector differing from the required fresh post-critic vector.)

Independent NumPy checks203745 native parameter partials(max2.46e-6),2470079
forward values(max5.45e-7),49 scalar finite differences, all174 Adam transitions
bit exactly and every phase's unselected owners. All2700 fitting visits and
accepted target words match. Disjoint per-class selected/unused IDs, domain
transforms, source-only G, image-only D, known diagnostic pixels, all validation
records and final-test loss/accuracy scalars pass. Original11 archives contain
4307530 exact values;363 phase/probe archives add2504554 exact values. The
original PNG, both TSVs and non-timing metrics match. Restored independent stores,
single/batch generation and all three invalid-domain controls pass.

The fixed-final result remains weak: reconstruction L1.438569665, G loss
6.36832428, D loss1.48392320 and generated requested-domain accuracy one third.
Valid conditioning and roundtrip arithmetic do not establish faithful translation,
class preservation or convergence. The report preserves all original panels and
adds all-digit diagnostics and fitting-only references. Canonical functionality
lives in the C++ API; Python/R expose the same owning live fields. Independent
full language fitting loops remain a separate migration task. Optional development
oracle: scripts/check_star_gan.py; native dataset preparation is part of the
complete program and does not require another checkout or Python data scripts.
